{{#contentFor "moHead"}}
<title>Complete Your Membership | Mere Orthodoxy</title>
<meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
<meta name="description" content="Add the print journal, the ebook library, audio essays, and the full member archive to your Mere Orthodoxy subscription." />
<meta property="og:title" content="Complete Your Membership" />
<meta property="og:description" content="Add the print journal, the ebook library, audio essays, and the full member archive to your Mere Orthodoxy subscription." />
<meta name="twitter:title" content="Complete Your Membership" />
<meta name="twitter:description" content="Add the print journal, the ebook library, audio essays, and the full member archive to your Mere Orthodoxy subscription." />
{{/contentFor}}
{{!-- /complete-membership/ — where a new Member lands after Portal checkout.

     One flow, one screen at a time, sharing the engine and the styles with
     /welcome/. Three kinds of step:

       address   the shipping address for the print journal. Always asked,
                 always first: it is the thing they just paid for and the
                 only step that is not optional. Posts to
                 /api/member/address, which needs street, city and postcode
                 together, so it saves only once all three exist.

       base      the six questions /welcome/ asks. A member who subscribed
                 free first has already answered these, so each one carries
                 data-answered-by and drops out if it is already on file.
                 Someone who went straight to paid answers them here, which
                 is how that cohort stops being a hole in the audience data.

       member    the two questions only members are asked. Wording is the
                 2026 member survey's, character for character, so answers
                 pool with the 186 responses already on the dashboard.

     Demographics post to /api/welcome-survey, NOT to the address endpoint.
     That is the change that makes them countable: the survey store is what
     produces Ghost labels and Kit tags and what the Audience board reads.
     The address endpoint keeps the address. --}}

{{#match @member.status "free"}}
  {{!-- Free subscribers don't get the print journal, and they answered the
       six base questions on /welcome/ already. Nothing to ask. --}}
  <main class="membership membership-support">
    <section class="page-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">Welcome to Mere Orthodoxy</p>
        <h1 class="page-hero-headline">You're <em>subscribed</em>.</h1>
        <p class="page-hero-sub">You'll receive the Weekly Digest in your inbox and can read every free essay online. Want the full experience, the print journal, the ebook library, audio versions, church calendar site themes, and the Member Dashboard? Upgrade any time.</p>
        <div class="button-row" style="margin-top: 24px;">
          <a href="/membership/" class="btn btn-primary btn-inline">Become a Member</a>
          <a href="https://mereorthodoxy.com" class="btn btn-dark btn-inline">Read Mere Orthodoxy</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
{{else}}
{{#if @member}}

